    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling core, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (71.91) and **Drake Baldwin** (70.41). **Gunnar Henderson** benefits significantly from a favorable park factor and a soft matchup against Springs, where he maintains his position in the heart of the order despite the dynamic platoon disadvantage. **Drake Baldwin** remains an elite start, as his role at the top of the lineup combined with a vulnerable 4.74 xERA from Adams provides a massive floor for runs scored. **Kyle Tucker** (70.18) also grades out as a top-tier play; despite a marginally unfavorable order spot, his ability to capitalize on Valdez\u2019s 4.40 xERA makes him a cornerstone for today\u2019s production. **Coby Mayo** (66.72) rounds out our strongest group, benefiting from an 8% boost due to his dynamic platoon advantage against a hittable starter.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was choosing between the bottom of our starting unit and **Miguel Vargas** (55.38). While **Miguel Vargas** presents a compelling case\u2014boasting an xwOBA of .373 and a slight boost for his ability to exploit a slow pitcher delivery\u2014his efficiency score fell just short of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Heliot Ramos**. We are leaning on **Luis Robert Jr.** (55.26) despite a platoon disadvantage because his base skill set remains too high to bench against Pecko\u2019s porous 6.99 xERA. We continue to monitor the status of **Andy Pages** and **Jacob Wilson** on the IL, but for now, the depth of our active roster, including **Sam Antonacci** and **Nasim Nunez**, provides enough speed-centric versatility to keep us competitive in our pursuit of the stolen base category. \n\nRisk management remains a priority given the volatility of the league\u2019s 5x5 landscape. While our hitters have favorable matchups, we must remain vigilant regarding the SP-xERA metrics for guys like **Jackson Merrill** (48.63) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (48.39), who are currently sitting in the marginal tier due to stiffer opposition. **Jackson Merrill** faces Rasmussen, whose 3.26 xERA acts as a significant drag on his score, and we have opted to limit his exposure today to preserve our remaining game caps. No major weather alerts are currently threatening play, but we are keeping a close watch on any lineup shifts that might impact the status of **Sam Antonacci** or **Drake Baldwin**, as their value is heavily tied to those leadoff spots.",
